<title>SWITZERLAND: BOE's Davies says BOE not trying to move sterling.</title>
<headline>BOE's Davies says BOE not trying to move sterling.</headline>
<dateline>DAVOS, Switzerland 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deputy governor Howard Davies said on Friday the Bank of England was not trying to move the level of sterling up or down against other currencies.</p>
<p>&quot;We are not actively seeking to influence the level of sterling at the moment in either way,&quot; Davies told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no firm view on where sterling should be...We have an inflation target regime, and that is what we look at,&quot; Davies said at the World Economic Forum in Davos.</p>
<p>-- Davos newsroom, +41-81-413 1449</p>
